{"availability":"available","full":"adieyal/transactions","name":"transactions","description":"Static browser app for exploring transactions, recurring spending, budgets, and forecasts","category":"Finance","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-30T01:00:49Z","updated":"2026-10-04T07:55:20Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://adieyal.github.io/transactions/","topics":[],"demo":"https://adieyal.github.io/transactions/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:41.720Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:41.720Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:41.720Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:41.720Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Transactions is a browser app for making sense of what you spend. A statement can show that in one month you paid a vet, a hardware shop and an airline. It can't show that the dog was ill, you were redoing the bathroom and you flew to a wedding. That context is what explains the numbers, and Transactions is built around adding it.","You start with your statements and shape the view around your own life. You decide how charges are grouped, using a short text list that you can change whenever your idea of a category changes. You mark the stretches of time that mattered, such as a trip, a move or the months of a renovation, and write down what was going on. When the reason for a charge isn't obvious, you add a note. Over time the timeline becomes a record of what happened, with the spending attached to it.","The calculations can be changed too. Each chart or table is a short JavaScript function you can read and edit. A question such as \"what did the renovation cost apart from the builder?\" can get its own view, written by you or by a connected assistant."],"features":["Each horizontal wire is a spending thread. Solid dots are imported charges; outlined dots mark refunds. Dashed marks show expected charges, and the shaded area marks future dates. Hover over a dot for a summary or click…","Choose Add statements and select a CSV, spreadsheet, text, or HTML statement. Recognized formats load directly; other files open a mapping dialog. Choose the date, merchant, and amount columns, check the date format and…","This screenshot maps the five rows in the sample CSV.","The Threads tab contains editable categorization rules. Write a thread name followed by indented merchant patterns or note tags. The first matching thread wins. A pattern such as harbor pantry matches that merchant;…","Add a monthly budget to the heading, for example Groceries [budget 300/month]. The timeline shows spending totals and budget progress. Edit the rules to match your own categories."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/adieyal/transactions/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"176375ff2129bd0793820cde196a0d0a5cfd08de4dc91adeac0a79a3d4bc2de3","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:12:00.009Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:12:00.009Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Transactions is a browser app for making sense of what you spend. A statement can show that in one month you paid a vet, a hardware shop and an airline. It can't show that the dog was ill, you were redoing the bathroom and you flew to a wedding. That context is what explains the numbers, and Transactions is built around adding it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/adieyal/transactions/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Open the AI settings to configure an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, model, and API key if the service requires one.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/adieyal/transactions/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"Live Claude account access and real AI credentials are not required by the automated tests.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/adieyal/transactions/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"176375ff2129bd0793820cde196a0d0a5cfd08d